sentences.l:
So she spoke, and he understood the voice of the goddess speaking,
and set out to run, and off he threw his cloak; and took care of it
the herald Eurybates of Ithaca, who kept him company;

“Strange man, sit still, and listen to the word of others,
who are stronger than you; and you are unwarlike and without might,
never once counted in war, nor in council;

let there be one ruler,
one king, to whom the son of Cronus of crooked cunning gave
the sceptre and the ordinances, that he may take counsel for them.”
